      "index": "b2m",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1613937795,
      "version": 734,
      "versionNonce": 950097261,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787439355175,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4) How we would ingest, transcode, package and deliver video to achieve smooth playback across many devices and network conditions\n(playback quality drives user satisfaction and cost)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "4) How we would ingest, transcode, package and deliver video to achieve smooth playback across many devices and network conditions\n(playback quality drives user satisfaction and cost)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "TVMXAFZE8Ma-ZTQiVIGP_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1094.2646518301794,
      "y": 1781.3283443687214,
      "width": 1236.526748307034,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2n",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 972574861,
      "version": 210,
      "versionNonce": 256009027,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787439375977,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Consider a pipeline that transcodes source mezzanine files into multiple resolutions/bitrates (ABR ladders) and packages\ninto HLS/DASH; you could generate captions, thumbnails, and trick-play sprites in the same pass.\n- Use a multi-CDN strategy with an origin store; minimize startup latency by using short initial segments, prefetching\nmanifests, and tuning segment durations.\n- Enforce DRM (e.g., Widevine/FairPlay/PlayReady) via a license service; bind licenses to entitlements and device capabilities,\nand fall back to lower bitrates or codecs when a device lacks support.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Consider a pipeline that transcodes source mezzanine files into multiple resolutions/bitrates (ABR ladders) and packages into HLS/DASH; you could generate captions, thumbnails, and trick-play sprites in the same pass.\n- Use a multi-CDN strategy with an origin store; minimize startup latency by using short initial segments, prefetching manifests, and tuning segment durations.\n- Enforce DRM (e.g., Widevine/FairPlay/PlayReady) via a license service; bind licenses to entitlements and device capabilities, and fall back to lower bitrates or codecs when a device lacks support.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "4UTxqTE7kqZ--BRSYhzu3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1109.9287142885385,
      "y": 1986.2773927074459,
      "width": 1092.2392578125,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2o",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1955670467,
      "version": 1011,
      "versionNonce": 76509421,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787439421187,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "5) Design recommendation engine to serve personalized homepage under tight latency while keeping results fresh",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "5) Design recommendation engine to serve personalized homepage under tight latency while keeping results fresh",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "OEUyyV3U40Hy3GdX8eiB-",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1091.2983578289177,
      "y": 2035.1260813088657,
      "width": 1090.9616812301465,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2p",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 887515693,
      "version": 93,
      "versionNonce": 1240351267,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787439603428,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Separate retrieval from ranking: you could fetch candidate sets by taste clusters or embeddings, then do\nlightweight online re-ranking with recent signals (session clicks, dwell time) and cache per-profile rows with\nshort TTLs.\n- Stream user events (views, clicks, searches) into an event bus so you can update features in near real time\nand trigger incremental jobs without coupling producers and consumers.\n- Plan for cold start and diversity: consider fallback heuristics (popular-in-region, new releases) and\nexplore/exploit logic to avoid echo chambers while staying within your latency budget.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Separate retrieval from ranking: you could fetch candidate sets by taste clusters or embeddings, then do lightweight online re-ranking with recent signals (session clicks, dwell time) and cache per-profile rows with short TTLs.\n- Stream user events (views, clicks, searches) into an event bus so you can update features in near real time and trigger incremental jobs without coupling producers and consumers.\n- Plan for cold start and diversity: consider fallback heuristics (popular-in-region, new releases) and explore/exploit logic to avoid echo chambers while staying within your latency budget.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Df0_TgB88lH66NOA13PbP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1112.8937802929693,
      "y": 2260.471728717363,
      "width": 1086.17919921875,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2q",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1788887373,
      "version": 1191,
      "versionNonce": 149096803,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787440016900,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "6) Enforce subscriptions, regional entitlement, concurrent stream/device limits without harming playback latency",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "6) Enforce subscriptions, regional entitlement, concurrent stream/device limits without harming playback latency",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "y-KYfeMqz6Vpuzgoopwha",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1115.028709839033,
      "y": 2297.463500588588,
      "width": 1197.535804572081,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2r",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1981027501,
      "version": 27,
      "versionNonce": 1967519267,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787440014965,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Issue short-lived playback tokens or DRM licenses after validating plan, region, and device; you could cache entitlements\nat the edge with aggressive TTLs and background refresh.\n- Track active sessions with per-account counters and expirations; consider atomic increments with leases and robust\ncleanup on crash/timeout to avoid phantom sessions.\n- Make payment and subscription changes idempotent and auditable; if a billing update spans multiple systems, use a\nworkflow or saga pattern for retries and compensations.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Issue short-lived playback tokens or DRM licenses after validating plan, region, and device; you could cache entitlements at the edge with aggressive TTLs and background refresh.\n- Track active sessions with per-account counters and expirations; consider atomic increments with leases and robust cleanup on crash/timeout to avoid phantom sessions.\n- Make payment and subscription changes idempotent and auditable; if a billing update spans multiple systems, use a workflow or saga pattern for retries and compensations.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "4l0FZZLeJhAPPKsr6Ley5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1118.6120008826408,
      "y": 2502.4274638243405,
      "width": 272.059814453125,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
